    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a really strong way to put it. so basically, it's pretty much universally accepted by historians that the labor movement was the driving force behind that stability, right? like, there aren't really any major arguments that suggest their influence was actually negative or caused more harm than good for the economy?",
